For middle rows, an additional character appears diagonally between consecutive vertical characters.
Algorithm
If numRows == 1, return the original string because no zigzag movement is needed.
Initialize an empty string res.
Calculate the cycle length using 2 * (numRows - 1).
Iterate through each row:
Start from the current row index.
Traverse the string using the cycle length as the increment.
Append the character at the current index.
For middle rows, calculate and append the diagonal character if it exists.
Return the resulting string.

